l Flush pattern focused on Bamboos (10 of my 14 tiles). The [T1, T2, T3] chow is complete but conflicts with the high-value flush pattern. However, discarding W7 first is the safest and most flexible choice - it maintains my complete [T1-T2-T3] chow while eliminating a useless isolated tile. All 4 copies of W7 are unshown, making it relatively safe to discard without feeding opponents. This keeps maximum flexibility to pivot toward either Half Flush (6 pts) or eventually Full Flush (24 pts) depending on draws.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
